# 01. Purpose

This document defines the security, safety, reliability, misuse, and operational risk architecture for AEGIS.

AEGIS is intended for high-stakes healthcare, biosecurity, pandemic preparedness, and biological resilience environments.

Because of that, the architecture must assume:

```text
systems fail
data can be wrong
sensors can fail
users can make mistakes
models can be wrong
integrations can fail
attackers exist
insiders exist
configurations drift
assumptions become outdated
```

The objective is not to create a system that never fails.

The objective is to create a system that:

```text
anticipates failure
detects failure
contains failure
communicates uncertainty
limits consequences
recovers safely
learns from failure
```

---

# 02. Core Risk Principle

AEGIS must be designed around:

> **Assume failure. Contain failure. Expose failure. Recover from failure. Learn from failure.**

A hidden failure is more dangerous than an obvious failure.

---

