# 43. Critical Action Protection

Consequential actions must require appropriate authorization.

Examples of potentially consequential operations include:

```text
changing operational controls
initiating restricted workflows
changing access permissions
publishing authoritative assessments
```

AEGIS should not assume that technical capability equals authorization.

---

# 44. Separation of Duties

Where appropriate, high-impact actions may require different roles for:

```text
analysis
approval
execution
review
```

The exact separation must be determined by stakeholder governance.

---

# 45. Insider Threat

AEGIS must consider malicious or careless insiders.

Controls include:

```text
least privilege
role separation
audit
anomaly detection
access reviews
privileged-user monitoring
```

---

# 46. Compromised Account

If an account is compromised, the attacker should not automatically gain unrestricted access.

Controls:

```text
least privilege
session controls
MFA
anomalous access detection
revocation
reauthentication
```

---

# 47. Supply Chain Risk

AEGIS depends on:

```text
libraries
frameworks
AI models
containers
cloud services
third-party APIs
development tools
```

Compromise of dependencies can compromise AEGIS.

Controls include:

```text
