Do not assume the original threat model remains complete.

---

# 95. Final Risk Principle

AEGIS must not be designed around the fantasy that:

> "If the software is correct, the system is safe."

A high-stakes system can fail even when the code works exactly as written.

The real risk surface includes:

```text
software
data
models
people
organizations
sensors
integrations
workflows
assumptions
```

Therefore:

> **AEGIS safety is a system property, not merely a software property.**

The strongest AEGIS architecture is one where a failure is:

```text
detected
understood
bounded
communicated
recoverable
auditable
learnable
```

rather than hidden behind a polished interface.
